  "scope_and_limitations": [
    "The main record is a same-client/same-payload A/A control. Baseline and candidate are execution-slot labels, not different software. No performance improvement is inferred from their differences.",
    "The PNG study uses the same client and native image with benchmark-only indexed-PNG level1 interposition. Exact decoded source pixels are preserved, WebP bytes are unchanged, and production compression defaults were not changed.",
    "Native libguac payload source is e1d2762776905f68b5a35b1b957b82b35a02311b/image737d50e9..., not a runtime comparison of private11native policy or live desktop capture/planning. Browser/harness source is0761e433...; bundle hashes are identical for both labels.",
    "Sender/source pacing target16ms is approximate. Timers sometimes wake early (worst1.474ms for source start in the control); release timing errors and actual gaps/rates are retained. Scheduled-source-due\u2192ACK is a scheduled-time/backlog proxy, not latency from an actual captured frame or kernel transmission.",
    "Application-level byte pacing/release delay/seeded jitter and unshaped loopback ACKs do not emulate Wi-Fi loss, TCP congestion, RTT, physical input or physical paint/FPS.",
    "Transfer overlaps decode. Browser first-img\u2192sync includes arrival/parsing/handlers; sync\u2192ACK includes remaining decode/frame wait/draw. Draw/handler aggregates overlap other intervals and are not independent additive stages.",
    "Exact per-frame RGBA checks run separately with ACK gating. Timed runs check final RGBA, all ordered draw coordinates/counts and exact ordered sync ACKs. A decoder-mode-specific reference is selected strictly by actual VideoFrame.format, never by pixel similarity or tolerance.",
    "PNG reference is independent Image/dataURI. WebP reference uses both CPU Image/RGB and complete-buffer native decode; the native reference is not an independent decoder algorithm. Canonical RGB/native canvas SHA256 values match across every source/payload label and run.",
    "Display queue snapshots omit partial/not-yet-arrived frames and can miss short spikes. Low display queue age does not establish low source-to-update latency; source schedule debt and actual transfer rates must be read alongside it.",
    "All p95 summaries here are arithmetic means of four per-run nearest-rank p95 values, not pooled percentiles. Short-run sub-ms label differences in this A/A control are not evidence of a speedup.",
    "One sequential encode_ms per exported asset is informational, excluded from browser/sender timing and not an encoder speed comparison. Candidate generic encoder_note is inherited; its explicit png_compression_control object authoritatively records level1 override."
  ],
